rate Investments segment to Supplies and Consumer Printing. The reporting change had no impact to previously reported consolidated net revenue, earnings from operations, net earnings or net earnings per share.</font></div><div style="height:42.75pt;position:relative;width:100%"><div style="bottom:0;position:absolute;width:100%"><div><font><br></font></div></div></div><div id="ibdc5bbc3a661442fbe3ac9ad52d08e6c_765"></div><hr style="page-break-after:always"><div style="min-height:42.75pt;width:100%"><div style="padding-left:18pt;text-indent:-18pt"><table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:74.025%"><tr><td style="width:1.0%"></td><td style="width:32.233%"></td><td style="width:0.1%"></td><td style="width:1.0%"></td><td style="width:32.233%"></td><td style="width:0.1%"></td><td style="width:1.0%"></td><td style="width:32.234%"></td><td style="width:0.1%"></td></tr><tr style="height:15pt"><td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"></td><td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"></td><td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt"></td></tr></table></div></div><div><table style="border-collapse:collapse;display:inline-table;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:98.115%"><tr><td style="width:1.0%"></td><td style="width:10.325%"></td><td style="width:0.1%"></td><td style="width:1.0%"></td><td style="width:76.048%"></td><td style="width:0.1%"></td><td style="width:1.0%"></td><td style="width:10.327%"></td><td style="width:0.1%"></td></tr><tr><td colspan="3" style="padding:0 1pt;vertical-align:bottom"><div style="text-align:center"><img alt="image9.jpg" src="image9.jpg" style="height:78px;margin-bottom:5pt;vertical-align:text-bottom;width:87px"></div></td><td colspan="3" style="padding:2px 1pt;text-align:center;vertical-align:middle"><font style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:100%">HP INC.&#160;AND SUBSIDIARIES<br>FISCAL 2024 SEGMENT INFORMATION (Revised)<br